        <h1>Terms &amp; conditions</h1>
        <p class="legal-intro">These terms apply to the TenderLens hackathon website, optional live search and account features. TenderLens is an early prototype, not a bidding or legal service.</p>
        <h2>Sample information</h2>
        <p>The sample tenders, buyers, values, dates, company profile and review results are fictional. They are included only to show how the website could work. Do not treat a sample status as a real eligibility result.</p>
        <h2>Live tender search</h2>
        <p>If the live search service is running, you can choose to send a search phrase and a portal to it. Search results may be incomplete, old or incorrect. Always open the official notice and check the latest documents yourself.</p>
        <h2>Strategy preview tools</h2>
        <p>The Strategy tools page builds a draft checklist, clarification prompts, capability-gap notes and an EMD cash scenario from values you enter. It does not read tender files, verify evidence, confirm that a consortium is permitted, or decide whether you qualify. The preview request is not stored by that route. Optional public-source search sends the tender title and selected portal to the configured search provider; results must be checked against official records.</p>
        <h2>Not legal or bid advice</h2>
        <p>TenderLens does not decide whether you should bid or whether you qualify. It does not guarantee that a tender is active, that every linked file was found, or that a requirement was understood correctly. Check the official documents and contact the buyer when something is unclear.</p>
        <h2>Prototype and account features</h2>
        <p>The sample tenders, report, filters, saved-example buttons and bidder checklist are illustrative. Sample results are not real eligibility decisions and sample saves stay in this browser for the current visit. When account sign-in is configured, Supabase Auth creates and manages your login. Supabase Postgres stores only the basic bidder profile you choose to save and live notice links that you explicitly save. Row-level security limits each account to its own records. Do not enter confidential business information.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for checking every official notice and deciding whether to bid. TenderLens does not confirm that a saved notice is still active. You can edit your profile or remove saved tender links from your account. Account deletion is not yet a self-service feature.</p>
        <h2>External providers</h2>
        <p>When you choose live search, the configured TenderLens server may use TinyFish to find public notices. Account sign-in and stored account data are provided by Supabase. Those providers have their own terms and privacy practices. The site loads the Supabase browser client from jsDelivr.</p>
        <h2>Using this preview</h2>
        <p>Use this website to explore the project and its sample interface. Do not rely on it for a purchase, bid, compliance decision or legal conclusion. The prototype is provided as-is while the team continues development.</p>
        <h2>Project contact</h2>
        <p>TenderLens is presented by TenderLens. No support address or commercial service has been provided.</p>
