      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="guide-main" id="main">
      <!-- HERO -->
      <section class="guide-hero">
        <div class="container guide-hero-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-mark"></span> STATUTORY PROCUREMENT PLAYBOOK &amp; EASY GUIDE</p>
            <h1>Master Indian Public Tenders in <em>six proven steps.</em></h1>
            <p class="guide-lede">From live portal discovery on GeM &amp; CPPP to Precedence DAG conflict resolution and GFR 2017 statutory bid pack generation—here is everything you need to know to qualify, challenge unlawful terms, and win public contracts.</p>
            <div class="guide-hero-actions">
              <a class="button button-primary" href="strategy.html" style="background: var(--green); color: #fff;">Launch Strategy Studio <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              <a class="button button-outline" href="index.html#opportunities">Explore Live Tenders <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-note">
            <span class="guide-note-icon" aria-hidden="true">🛡</span>
            <div>
              <p><strong>Deterministic Statutory Proof</strong><br>Indian procurement laws mandate statutory exemptions for Startups &amp; MSMEs. TenderLens evaluates every clause with mathematical logic and source citations—with zero LLM guessing.</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6-STEP PLAYBOOK CARDS -->
      <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="guide-section-header">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">01 / THE TENDERLENS PLAYBOOK</p>
              <h2 id="steps-title">Six steps to qualification &amp; bid readiness</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="guide-section-intro">TenderLens bridges the asymmetric information gap between government buyers and ambitious bidders through deterministic evidence and statutory defense.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="guide-step-grid">
            <!-- Step 1 -->
            <article class="guide-step-card">
              <div class="guide-step-card-top">
                <span class="guide-step-num">1</span>
                <span class="guide-step-tag">DISCOVERY ENGINE</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Real-Time Portal Discovery</h3>
              <p>Search active tenders across GeM, CPPP, and State eProcurement portals using TinyFish live intelligence. Automatically ingest tender notices, technical specifications, and corrigenda attachments.</p>
              <div class="guide-step-card-footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="index.html#opportunities">Discover live tenders <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Step 2 -->
            <article class="guide-step-card">
              <div class="guide-step-card-top">
                <span class="guide-step-num">2</span>
                <span class="guide-step-tag">PRECEDENCE DAG</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Resolve Contradictory Clauses</h3>
              <p>Indian tenders span multiple PDFs. TenderLens builds a Directed Acyclic Graph where Rank 1 Corrigenda strictly supersede earlier terms, preventing you from being misled by obsolete turnover or EMD demands.</p>
              <div class="guide-step-card-footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="strategy.html#precedence-rag-workbench">Test Precedence DAG <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Step 3 -->
            <article class="guide-step-card">
              <div class="guide-step-card-top">
                <span class="guide-step-num">3</span>
                <span class="guide-step-tag">DETERMINISTIC GATES</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Audit Core Qualifications</h3>
              <p>Execute zero-hallucination mathematical verification across 3-year turnover, operating experience, EMD exemption rules, Class-I/II Make in India local content, and CPWD 80/50/40 similar-work ratios.</p>
              <div class="guide-step-card-footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="strategy.html">Run qualification audit <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Step 4 -->
            <article class="guide-step-card">
              <div class="guide-step-card-top">
                <span class="guide-step-num">4</span>
                <span class="guide-step-tag">STATUTORY SHIELD</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Defeat Illegal Buyer Revocations</h3>
              <p>Detect and strike down ultra vires buyer ATC clauses that attempt to cancel startup/MSME exemptions in violation of GFR 2017 Rule 173(i) and GeM General Terms Clause 4(xiii)(h).</p>
              <div class="guide-step-card-footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="#statutory-shield-guide">Inspect startup shield <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Step 5 -->
            <article class="guide-step-card">
              <div class="guide-step-card-top">
                <span class="guide-step-num">5</span>
                <span class="guide-step-tag">ZERO-HISTORY MERIT</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Prove Technical Equivalence</h3>
              <p>When you have zero corporate operating history, TenderLens evaluates plant machinery, testing standards, and team pedigree to generate an official Annexure-I Quality Control Proforma.</p>
              <div class="guide-step-card-footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="strategy.html">Generate QC proforma <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Step 6 -->
            <article class="guide-step-card">
              <div class="guide-step-card-top">
                <span class="guide-step-num">6</span>
                <span class="guide-step-tag">PDF BID PACK</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Export Portal-Ready PDFs</h3>
              <p>Download signed-ready PDF undertakings for Bid Security Declarations (GFR 170(i)), Make in India local content self-certifications, Land Border compliance, and complete final bid packs.</p>
              <div class="guide-step-card-footer">
                <a class="text-link" href="strategy.html">Download PDF bid pack <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- PRECEDENCE DAG HIERARCHY MAP -->
      <section class="guide-section guide-section-muted" aria-labelledby="precedence-map-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">02 / DOCUMENT HIERARCHY</p>
            <h2 id="precedence-map-title">How Indian legal precedence works</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">In Indian administrative law, contradictory terms across tender PDFs are resolved by strict hierarchical order. TenderLens constructs a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) to enforce this deterministically:</p>
            <div class="guide-final-links" style="margin-top: 24px;">
              <a class="button button-dark" href="strategy.html#precedence-rag-workbench">Launch DAG Workbench <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-hierarchy-card">
            <div class="hierarchy-item hierarchy-rank-1">
              <div class="hierarchy-badge">RANK 1</div>
              <div class="hierarchy-content">
                <h4>Corrigenda &amp; Official Amendments</h4>
                <p>Governing authority over all prior documents. Any change to dates, turnover criteria, or EMD terms immediately negates earlier clauses.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="hierarchy-connector">↓ overrides</div>
            <div class="hierarchy-item hierarchy-rank-2">
              <div class="hierarchy-badge">RANK 2</div>
              <div class="hierarchy-content">
                <h4>GeM General Terms &amp; Conditions (GTC)</h4>
                <p>Statutory baseline for all public buying. Protects statutory exemptions (Clauses 4(xiii)(h), 4(xxii)) against buyer violations.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="hierarchy-connector">↓ overrides</div>
            <div class="hierarchy-item hierarchy-rank-3">
              <div class="hierarchy-badge">RANK 3</div>
              <div class="hierarchy-content">
                <h4>Buyer Additional Terms &amp; Conditions (ATC)</h4>
                <p>Custom buyer requirements. Valid only if they do NOT conflict with GeM GTC or Government of India public procurement policies.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="hierarchy-connector">↓ overrides</div>
            <div class="hierarchy-item hierarchy-rank-4">
              <div class="hierarchy-badge">RANK 4</div>
              <div class="hierarchy-content">
                <h4>Consortium &amp; Joint Venture Frameworks</h4>
                <p>Defines prime bidder and subcontractor role distributions, split-turnover aggregations, and technical responsibilities.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="hierarchy-connector">↓ overrides</div>
            <div class="hierarchy-item hierarchy-rank-5">
              <div class="hierarchy-badge">RANK 5</div>
              <div class="hierarchy-content">
                <h4>Main RFP / Tender Notice</h4>
                <p>Baseline initial tender scope. Completely superseded whenever an amendment or corrigendum is issued.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5-PILLAR ARCHITECTURE REVIEW -->
      <section class="guide-section" id="strategy-tools" aria-labelledby="strategy-guide-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="guide-section-header">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">03 / THE 5 STRATEGY PILLARS</p>
              <h2 id="strategy-guide-title">Comprehensive statutory toolkit</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="guide-section-intro">Built to transform legal complexity into actionable, defensible bid submissions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-pillar-grid">
            <article class="guide-pillar-card">
              <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
              <h3>Pre-Bid Legal Pack</h3>
              <p>Auto-drafts formal representation letters citing CVC Office Memorandum No. 12-02-1-CTE-6 and Ministry of Finance guidelines to challenge anti-competitive buyer terms during the pre-bid clarification window.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="guide-pillar-card">
              <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
              <h3>Consortium Matchmaker</h3>
              <p>Quantifies exact eligibility shortfalls across turnover, operating years, and manufacturing capacity. Recommends optimal Joint Venture (JV) and OEM subcontractor partner archetypes.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="guide-pillar-card">
              <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
              <h3>Compliance Matrix &amp; Affidavits</h3>
              <p>Generates clause-by-clause compliance tables, downloadable CSV matrices, and official PDF statutory undertakings: Bid Security, Local Content, Land Border, and QC Proforma.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="guide-pillar-card">
              <div class="pillar-num">04</div>
              <h3>EMD Capital Optimizer</h3>
              <p>Calculates effective cash lock-up, working capital cost, and exercises statutory rights to submit IRDAI Insurance Surety Bonds or GFR 170(i) MSME exemption declarations.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="guide-pillar-card">
              <div class="pillar-num">05</div>
              <h3>Rejection Forensics</h3>
              <p>Scans historical rejection checkpoints from past GeM and CPPP technical bids to protect you from common clerical pitfalls (missing ICAI UDIN, outdated OEM authorization formats).</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ZERO-HISTORY STARTUP EXEMPTION GUIDE -->
      <section class="guide-section guide-section-muted" id="statutory-shield-guide" aria-labelledby="shield-guide-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">04 / ZERO-HISTORY STARTUP EXEMPTION</p>
            <h2 id="shield-guide-title">How to bid on ₹10Cr+ tenders with ₹0 revenue</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">If your company is under 10 years old and registered with DPIIT, Indian public procurement law gives you statutory exemptions from prior turnover and experience.</p>
            <div class="guide-final-links" style="margin-top: 24px;">
              <a class="button button-primary" href="strategy.html" style="background: var(--green); color: #fff;">Test in Strategy Studio <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-setup">
            <ol>
              <li><strong>GFR 2017 Rule 173(i) Waiver:</strong> Ministry of Finance mandates that prior turnover and prior experience are waived for recognized startups, subject to technical specifications.</li>
              <li><strong>Technical Equivalence over Past Revenue:</strong> Instead of past balance sheets, provide government-accredited lab test reports (NABL, BIS, STQC) proving your product meets specifications.</li>
              <li><strong>Annexure-I Quality Control Proforma:</strong> TenderLens automatically drafts the official equipment and quality assurance affidavit that protects the government buyer from audit inquiries.</li>
              <li><strong>Pre-Bid Legal Representation:</strong> If a buyer attempts to write "No startup exemption" in the fine print, TenderLens auto-drafts a formal challenge letter citing GeM GTC Clause 4(xiii)(h) to remove the unfair barrier.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="guide-warning"><strong>Statutory Ground:</strong> Ministry of Finance Department of Expenditure OM F.20/2/2014-PPD(Pt.) explicitly prohibits procuring entities from diluting or denying startup exemptions in public tenders.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- MANDATORY 25% MSE SUBCONTRACTING -->
      <section class="guide-section" id="mse-quota-guide" aria-labelledby="mse-quota-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">05 / MANDATORY 25% MSE SUBCONTRACTING</p>
            <h2 id="mse-quota-title">Claim the mandatory 25% MSE subcontracting quota on mega tenders</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">Even when a tender is too large (e.g. ₹50 Crore) for a small firm to bid as prime contractor, the law guarantees you a 25% share.</p>
            <div class="guide-final-links" style="margin-top: 24px;">
              <a class="button button-dark" href="strategy.html">Calculate Your 25% Quota <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-setup account-setup-card">
            <ol>
              <li><strong>The ₹2 Crore Mandatory Trigger:</strong> Under Section 4 of the Public Procurement Policy for MSEs Order 2012, any Central Government procurement valued at or above ₹200 Lakhs (₹2 Crore) mandates that the winning prime contractor must subcontract at least 25% of the total order value to registered Micro &amp; Small Enterprises.</li>
              <li><strong>L1 + 15% Split-Order Purchase Preference:</strong> When an MSE quotes within 15% of the lowest non-MSE bid (L1), the MSE has the statutory right to match L1's price and win 25% of the order quantity.</li>
              <li><strong>Ready-to-Send Partnership Outreach:</strong> TenderLens auto-generates a formal tripartite partnership agreement citing the statutory 25% quota to present to prime EPC bidders.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="guide-warning"><strong>Debarment Protection:</strong> Prime contractors who fail to fulfill their 25% MSE subcontracting quota face contract cancellation and debarment under GeM GTC Clause 4(xxii).</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- GLOSSARY -->
      <section class="guide-section guide-section-muted" aria-labelledby="words-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">06 / PROCUREMENT GLOSSARY</p>
            <h2 id="words-title">Statutory terms &amp; definitions</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">Indian public procurement relies on specific statutory definitions. Here are the authoritative standards used in TenderLens.</p>
          </div>
          <dl class="guide-glossary">
            <div><dt>Corrigendum</dt><dd>An official gazetted amendment that overrides, modifies, or cancels earlier tender terms. Has Rank 1 legal precedence.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>ATC</dt><dd>Additional Terms and Conditions: custom rules specified by the buyer. Legally void if they contradict GeM GTC or GFR statutory exemptions.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>GTC</dt><dd>General Terms &amp; Conditions: the overarching platform contract governing all transactions on Government e-Marketplace (GeM).</dd></div>
            <div><dt>GFR 2017</dt><dd>General Financial Rules, 2017: statutory procurement rules issued by the Ministry of Finance governing all Central Government expenditure.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Rule 170(i)</dt><dd>Statutory provision granting full Earnest Money Deposit (EMD) exemption to Micro &amp; Small Enterprises and recognized Startups.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Rule 173(i)</dt><dd>Mandates that prior turnover and operating experience criteria must be relaxed for recognized Startups &amp; MSEs.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Class-I Local Supplier</dt><dd>A supplier whose goods or services offer local value addition equal to or exceeding 50% under the DPIIT Make in India Order.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Insurance Surety Bond</dt><dd>An IRDAI-approved guarantee instrument permitted under GFR Rule 170(i) in lieu of costly bank guarantees and fixed deposits.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- REFINED ENTERPRISE ADVISORY CARD -->
      <section class="guide-section">
        <div class="container guide-final-card">
          <div class="guide-final-card-body">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-mark"></span> ENTERPRISE STATUTORY ADVISORY</p>
            <h2>Ready to evaluate your tender with deterministic proof?</h2>
            <p>Run your active tender PDF or bidder profile through the deterministic qualification engine to resolve document precedence, audit statutory exemptions, and generate portal-ready PDF submission packs in seconds.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-final-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="strategy.html" style="background: var(--green); color: #fff;">Launch Strategy Studio <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a class="button button-outline" href="index.html#opportunities">Explore Live Tenders <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
