      <section class="intro-section section-rule" id="approach">
        <div class="container intro-grid">
          <div class="section-aside"><span class="section-number">02 / THE PROBLEM</span><span class="aside-rule"></span><span class="aside-note">A tender is rarely one document.</span></div>
          <div class="intro-main">
            <p class="eyebrow">The hard part comes after discovery</p>
            <h2>The clause that changes everything may be in the <em>third file.</em></h2>
            <p class="intro-body">A tender can spread its rules across several files. The buyer may add extra terms, and an official update may change them later. TenderLens is designed to bring those files together and show what changed.</p>
